Major changes made by this fork
-------------------------------

The MIT License permits derivative works. For traceability, the following are
the substantial changes made relative to the upstream code base. This list is
informative, not a warranty of completeness.

  1. Third user-interface locale: Vietnamese (`vi`).
     - New locale tree under `frontend/src/i18n/locales/vi/`, registered in
       `frontend/src/i18n/detect.ts` and `frontend/src/i18n/messages.ts`.
     - The default locale is now `vi`; `en` is the secondary locale.
     - `zh` is retained for ENUM-valued data, API payloads, and stored records.
     - The language switcher exposes `vi` / `en` / `zh`.
     - Web font subsets: Noto Sans (Latin Extended, for `vi`) alongside
       Noto Sans SC / Noto Serif SC (for `zh`).

  2. New visual design system.
     - Replacement stylesheets and semantic class naming for the user-facing
       application, replacing the upstream presentation layer.
     - The admin console keeps its own Tailwind design system.

  3. Operations documentation.
     - `docs/OPERATIONS.md` — architecture, configuration, task lifecycle,
       billing, model routing, payment, media storage, deployment, and
       troubleshooting. Written from the actual code in this repository.
     - `docs/OPEN_SOURCE_CHECKLIST.md` — itemised audit of licence, trademark,
       asset-provenance, secret-leak, provider-lock, and third-party-dependency
       items, each with a status and a decision that a human still has to make.
     - `docs/VI_BACKLOG.md` — measured inventory of remaining Chinese text in
       the backend, admin console, and frontend.
     - `docs/ADMIN_I18N_PLAN.md` — plan for localisation of the admin console.
     - Rewritten `README.md` and `docs/STANDARDS.md`; updated `CLAUDE.md`.

  4. Dead-code removal and comment localisation.
     - Removal of unused frontend exports that were byte-for-byte duplicates of
       `frontend/src/i18n/locales/*/pages.ts` content.
     - Translation of backend source comments and docstrings from Chinese into
       Vietnamese, restricted to the core backend modules. User-facing runtime
     strings, API values, log messages, and e-mail bodies are deliberately left
       unchanged.

  5. Rebranding.
     - The product is presented under its own name, with its own logo, copy,
     and documentation. Upstream marks are being retired item by item; see
     `docs/OPEN_SOURCE_CHECKLIST.md`.

